-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. Two traces of one contract whose `buy` is allowed only
-- while `taken now`, a rule of taken.l4 with no inputs that reads the ledger,
-- is false. The first trace (peek) reads `taken now` before `taken` is
-- committed. The second (skip) commits `taken` at once, so its `buy` is passed
-- over, as it is when that trace is run alone (one COMMIT, WITHIN 9). Each
-- #TRACE has a ledger of its own, and each must read an imported rule afresh.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
